/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
45 780 Td
(   structure\).) Tj
T*
(   - Cataphoric Reference \(Forward-Looking Specification\):) Tj
T*
(   - The referent's identity is established by a modifier that immediately follows the noun phrase) Tj
T*
(   \(e.g., prepositional phrases, relative clauses\):) Tj
T*
(   - Text: "The concentration of the solute in the test tube was monitored." \(Identified by 'of) Tj
T*
(   the solute'\).) Tj
T*
(   - Text: "The vector that was transformed into E. coli contained kanamycin resistance.") Tj
T*
(   \(Identified by the relative clause\).) Tj
T*
(   - Text: "The hypothesis that retroviruses cause oncogenesis gained widespread clinical) Tj
T*
(   backing.") Tj
T*
(   - Exophoric Reference \(Situational / Shared World Knowledge\):) Tj
T*
(   - Refers to entities universally known to exist uniquely, or entities immediately obvious in) Tj
T*
(   the physical room/environment:) Tj
T*
(   - Text: "The Sun emits ionizing radiation", "The atmosphere", "The laboratory technician) Tj
T*
(   calibrated the hood".) Tj
T*
(   - Shared Laboratory Context: "Please autoclave the waste canisters" \(Both speaker and listener) Tj
T*
(   know which canisters are in the cleanroom\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 3:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the rules governing Zero Article \(omission of articles\) with uncountable nouns, plural nouns, and academic disciplines.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Zero Article Rule:) Tj
T*
(   The zero article \(absence of a, an, or the\) occurs in formal English to denote generic) Tj
T*
(   reference across broad categories:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Core Academic Categories Requiring Zero Article:) Tj
T*
(   - Uncountable \(Mass\) Nouns in Generic Statements:) Tj
T*
(   - Expresses general truths about chemical substances, physical states, or biochemical) Tj
T*
(   macromolecules:) Tj
T*
(   - Correct: "DNA stores genetic information." \(Not *The DNA stores...\).) Tj
T*
(   - Correct: "Water freezes at 0 deg C under standard atmospheric conditions.") Tj
T*
(   - Correct: "Lipids constitute the hydrophobic core of cellular membranes.") Tj
T*
(   - Contrast Specific Reference: "The DNA extracted from sample B was degraded.") Tj
T*
(   - Plural Countable Nouns in Generic Statements:) Tj
T*
(   - Refers to an entire class of organisms or objects:) Tj
T*
(   - Correct: "Bacteriophages infect bacterial host cells." \(Not *The bacteriophages...\).) Tj
T*
(   - Correct: "Antibodies bind antigens with stereospecific affinity.") Tj
T*
(   - Correct: "Plasmids serve as versatile vectors in genetic engineering.") Tj
T*
(   - Academic Disciplines and Fields of Study:) Tj
T*
(   - Correct: "He specializes in Bioinformatics and Structural Biology." \(Never *the) Tj
T*
(   bioinformatics\).) Tj
T*
(   - Correct: "Biochemical engineering bridges microbiology and fluid dynamics.") Tj
T*
(   - Diseases and Pathologies:) Tj
T*
(   - Correct: "The patient was treated for leukemia." \(Not *the leukemia\).) Tj
T*
(   - Correct: "Hepatitis C is caused by an enveloped RNA virus.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Contextual Contrast Heuristic:) Tj
T*
(   Whenever a mass or plural noun is restricted by a specific descriptive phrase or environmental) Tj
T*
(   container, zero article reverts to the definite article 'the':) Tj
T*
(   - Generic: "Buffer maintains enzymatic stability.") Tj
T*
(   - Specific: "The buffer inside reactor vessel 2 was depleted.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
