BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Examine the definite article 'the' with inventions, scientific instruments, and physiological systems.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Archetypal Definite Article for Inventions:) Tj
T*
(   When an invention, musical instrument, or scientific apparatus is viewed as a monumental) Tj
T*
(   technological milestone rather than an individual piece of glass and metal, it takes the) Tj
T*
(   generic definite article 'the':) Tj
T*
(   - "The telescope transformed our perception of the cosmos.") Tj
T*
(   - "The thermal cycler revolutionized molecular cloning.") Tj
T*
(   - "The flow cytometer enabled single-cell immunology.") Tj
T*
(   - Contrast Individual Object: "The technician dropped a thermal cycler on the floor." \(Refers) Tj
T*
(   to one specific physical machine\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Anatomical and Physiological Systems:) Tj
T*
(   Major physiological organ systems consistently take the definite article:) Tj
T*
(   - "The central nervous system", "The immune system", "The cardiovascular system", "The Krebs) Tj
T*
(   cycle", "The electron transport chain".) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 16:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the syntax of 'Both', 'Neither', and 'Either' with dual biological samples and bilateral structures.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Dual Grammatical System:) Tj
T*
(   English preserves a dedicated dual grammatical category for pairs of entities:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Structural Formulations:) Tj
T*
(   - Both \(Affirmative inclusive - takes plural noun and plural verb\):) Tj
T*
(   - Determiner: "Both kidneys were examined for histopathological lesions.") Tj
T*
(   - Predeterminer: "Both the kidneys were examined.") Tj
T*
(   - Pronoun: "Both were functional.") Tj
T*
(   - Either \(Disjunctive alternative - takes singular noun and singular verb\):) Tj
T*
(   - Determiner: "Either kidney was sufficient to sustain normal renal clearance.") Tj
T*
(   - Disjunctive pair: "Either kidney A or kidney B was harvested.") Tj
T*
