(   Uncombined chemical elements, gases, and simple compounds function as mass nouns and take ZERO) Tj
T*
(   article in general chemical discourse:) Tj
T*
(   - "Oxygen and hydrogen combine to form water.") Tj
T*
(   - "Carbon is the backbone of organic chemistry.") Tj
T*
(   - "Ethanol was used to precipitate nucleic acids.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Specific Chemical Ions and Functional Groups:) Tj
T*
(   When referring to discrete structural chemical entities or ions, the definite article is) Tj
T*
(   required:) Tj
T*
(   - "The hydroxyl group \(-OH\) participates in hydrogen bonding.") Tj
T*
(   - "The phosphate backbone confers a net negative charge to DNA.") Tj
T*
(   - "The sodium ion \(Na+\) is pumped against its concentration gradient.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Bounded Reagents:) Tj
T*
(   - "Add 10 mL of ethanol." \(Zero article\).) Tj
T*
(   - "The ethanol used in this step was chilled to -20 deg C." \(Definite article\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
