BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the syntax and semantics of 'A number of' versus 'The number of' in clinical trial reporting.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. 'A Number of' \(Plural Idiomatic Quantifier\):) Tj
T*
(   - Meaning: Equivalent to 'several', 'multiple', or 'many'.) Tj
T*
(   - Grammatical Status: The noun following 'of' is the true semantic head; mandates a PLURAL) Tj
T*
(   verb:) Tj
T*
(   - "A number of patients experienced mild transient erythema at the injection site.") Tj
T*
(   - "A number of false-positive readings were eliminated by re-calibration.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. 'The Number of' \(Singular Numerical Metric\):) Tj
T*
(   - Meaning: Refers to the specific abstract mathematical figure, count, or total sum.) Tj
T*
(   - Grammatical Status: 'Number' is the singular grammatical head; mandates a SINGULAR verb:) Tj
T*
(   - "The number of patients enrolled in cohort A was forty-eight.") Tj
T*
(   - "The number of viable bacterial colonies decreases exponentially with heat exposure.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 23:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Examine article usage with unique administrative, institutional, and academic titles \(e.g., PI, Director, Dean\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Unique Roles as Subject:) Tj
T*
(   When referencing an individual holding a unique organizational post as the subject of a clause,) Tj
T*
(   the definite article 'the' is mandatory:) Tj
T*
(   - "The Principal Investigator approved the modification of the animal protocol.") Tj
T*
(   - "The Dean of Engineering dedicated the new bioprocess pilot facility.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Predicative Complements After Verbs of Appointment:) Tj
T*
(   When a unique administrative post follows verbs such as appoint, elect, declare, make, or) Tj
T*
(   designate, the article is conventionally OMITTED \(Zero Article\):) Tj
T*
(   - "Dr. Sharma was appointed Principal Investigator of the CAR-T project." \(Not *appointed the) Tj
T*
(   Principal Investigator\).) Tj
T*
(   - "She was elected Chairperson of the Institutional Biosafety Committee." \(Not *elected the) Tj
T*
(   Chairperson\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 24:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze determiner syntax with 'Another', 'Other', 'The other', and 'Others' in comparative laboratory trials.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Morphological Breakdown:) Tj
T*
(   - Another \(An + other\): Applied strictly to singular countable nouns \("another plasmid",) Tj
T*
(   "another test tube"\). Never write *another plasmids.) Tj
T*
(   - Other: Applied to plural countable nouns or mass nouns without articles \("other researchers",) Tj
T*
(   "other data"\).) Tj
T*
(   - The other: Refers to the remaining member of a known pair or specific set:) Tj
T*
(   - "One aliquot was frozen; the other aliquot was incubated at 37 deg C.") Tj
T*
(   - Others / The others: Nominal pronouns functioning without following nouns:) Tj
T*
ET

